Theodore Reed wrote:
> 13:27 < treed> I'm past wanting to tinker with the language. I'd like to 
> just be able to use it and not have to worry that some asshat's going to 
> come along and dick with my shit.
> 13:28 < treed> If it weren't for outstanding broken bullshit, I'd just 
> suggest that we declare the time for tinkering over.
> 13:29 < treed> And ignore the tinkerers henceforth.

%^)

We did declare the time for tinkering over.  Back in 1997 wen CLL came 
out.  It became the current language baseline.

I have been saying the above since then.  xorlo was approved anyway.

Unfortunately, the tinkerers have a different concept of what 
constitutes "outstanding broken bullshit" than you and I do.  Because we 
haven't gotten the BYFY project done, we can't redeclare the baseline, 
and the proposals keep coming.

We really have to finish defining the current language.  Then decide if 
anything is broken enough to be worth fixing.  Then fix it and be done.

Then the tinkerers can be successfully ignored.

lojbab
